{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require SEND & neurodevelopmental training for social & family help workers",
        "additional_details": "Children with autism, ADHD, communication differences, developmental delay, sensory needs or EBSA can sometimes present in ways that overlap with signs of neglect or parenting difficulties. \r\n \r\nWithout specialist SEND knowledge, there is a risk these needs may be misunderstood. We want mandatory SEND and neurodevelopmental training, so practitioners know what to recognise, what support to seek, and when specialist input is needed before life-changing safeguarding decisions are made.",
        "background": "Mandate SEND and neurodevelopmental training for children\u2019s social workers and Family Help practitioners who carry out or contribute to safeguarding, neglect or parenting-capacity assessments.",
